dividual medley and the 4x100 metre freestyle relay added. In addition, the 100 metre backstroke was eliminated, but was replaced by the 200 metre backstroke. Women had 8 events in 1964, adding the 400 individual medley."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The United States dominance in 1964 swimming was almost complete, winning 13 of 18 gold medals, and 29 of 54 available medals. Their men won 7 of 10 events and 14 of 30 medals, while the US women won 6 of 8 events and 15 of 24 medals."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51552"} "Don Schollander"] " (USA) was the swim star of the 1964 Olympics, winning four gold medals, even though his best event, the 200 freestyle, was not yet on the Olympic Program. Two other Americans, " [:a {:href "/athletes/51207"} "Sharon Stouder"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/51294"} "Steve Clark"] ", won three gold medals. Three swimmers besides Schollander won four medals – Stouder, " [:a {:href "/athletes/51011"} "Kathy Ellis"] " (USA), and " [:a {:href "/athletes/47851"} "Hans-Joachim Klein"] " (GER)."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5654"} "100 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "11 – 12 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "66"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5670"} "400 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "14 – 15 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "49"] "\n" [:td {} "27"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5680"} "1,500 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "16 – 17 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "31"] "\n" [:td {} "21"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5728"} "4 × 100 metres Freestyle Relay, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "13 – 14 October 1964"]